WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:04.300
-Joe. I'm excited you're here.
We're gonna talk sneakers.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.767
I want to talk about
all this stuff.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:08.934
And we actually might even show
what may be Sneaker of the Year.

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:10.267
-Maybe. Yes.
-We're not sure. Yeah.

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:11.567
-We're gonna debate it
right here.

00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:13.667
-What got you interested?
Do you remember?

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:15.701
Like, what got you started
with sneakers?

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:17.133
-I was always into sneakers.

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:20.734
And then my first job, 16,
was at a sneaker store.

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:22.667
Finish Line.
South Shore Mall in Bay Shore.

00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:24.501
Shout-out to my hometown.
-Yeah.

00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:27.834
-And it was funny because, like,
the screening process

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:30.934
to get the job wasn't, like,
you have to interview.

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:33.467
It was literally like,
"Hey, this store is opening up.

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:37.634
Put your name and birthday
on a 8x11 sheet of paper."

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:39.133
And if you could do that,
you're hired.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:40.801
-Yeah. There you go.
And you did that?

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:42.701
-I did that correctly.
I did that correctly.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.200
But it was awesome
because, like,

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.200
I worked with, like,
all my track team.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.434
It was, like, my first job,

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:49.133
and it was like 20 of us
are working there.

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.367
-That's the best.
-They lasted like 2 or 3 months

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:54.000
and I lasted like 8 years,
on and off, so...

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.534
-You really got dedicated.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:58.934
-And do you remember --
do you remember

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.734
the first pair of sneakers
that got you excited?

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.801
-My parents were really good
because they, like,

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:07.067
got me the one pair every year
that was, like, the pair.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.601
May have been, like,
only one pair a year,

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:11.767
but it was, like, the pair,
first day of school.

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:14.334
I remember in ninth grade,
in 1997,

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:15.901
the Air Max 97 came out.

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.200
Great, great shoe.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.000
I'm sure Quest knows.
Quest is a big sneakerhead.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.234
-Yes, he is. Yeah. Tariq, too.
-And -- Exactly.

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:26.334
Tariq, as well.
And the Air Max 97.

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:28.000
I remember, like,
the first day of school.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.133
Ninth grade, you're always
nervous to go to high school,

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:32.467
and, like, I, like,
laid out the outfit

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:34.734
and had the Air Max 97
with, like, the --

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:37.267
It was like a person
in my bedroom just laid out.

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.200
-Oh, yeah.
-And the shoes at the bottom.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.334
So that one -- that sticks out
when I was like 14 or 15.

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:45.434
-Yeah. Did you keep --
Do you keep the box?

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:49.901
-I keep the boxes now, but they
take up too much room now.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:52.000
-Oh, now. Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I remember. Yeah.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.400
I didn't really have
the greatest sneakers growing up

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.834
because I kept
growing out of them.

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:58.434
My parents were getting mad.
They were like, "Stop growing.

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:00.334
It's costing us too much money."

00:02:00.334 --> 00:02:01.934
-And they take up
a lot of space.

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:04.300
Yeah. So they were like -- Yeah.
I had, like, one pair

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.133
and I would, like,
squeeze out of them.

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:08.234
They're like, "Alright. Fine.
Let's get him, you know..."

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:11.367
But I remember when I --
when I did stand-up,

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:12.901
I would wear Nikes

00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:15.801
because Jerry Seinfeld
wore Nikes on "Seinfeld."

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:18.467
And so I go, "That's good luck.
I'm going to wear Nikes."

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:20.133
And that was my thing
for a while.

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:22.434
-So I need, like,
a favor from you

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:24.434
because he hasn't done
"Sneaker Shopping" yet.

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:27.000
And Jerry -- What you just said.
Jerry is known --

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.534
On "Seinfeld," he had, like
such classic '90s sneakers,

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:33.067
and they were switching it out
almost like every episode.

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:34.701
-Yeah.
-Can you put in the word?

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:36.434
-Yeah.
Can you put in the word?

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:37.901
-Yes. He would be a great guest.
Jerry.

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:40.267
You got to do "Sneaker Shopping"
with Joe La Puma.

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:43.567
You got to do it.
-We need it. We need it.

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:47.367
-We have some --
We have some sneakers here.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.467
Explain to me. What are these?

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:52.167
-So, we just had DJ Khaled
on this week's episode.

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:54.133
-He's the best.
-The best. The best.

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:55.534
-What did he call you?

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:58.133
-He called me Jay Pluma.
Fine. It's okay.

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.501
-Jay Pluma?
-Yeah.

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:01.334
Instead of Joe La Puma,
he called me Jay Pluma.

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:02.901
It's fine. If anyone can get --

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:04.868
If anyone can get away with it,
it's DJ Khaled.

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:07.367
But he's been here,
and you know his energy.

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:10.501
When you film with DJ Khaled,
he's the host,

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:11.701
he's the producer,

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:14.300
he's the director,
and he's the guest.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.000
-He's everything.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.334
-So you just have to keep --
-He's the camera operator.

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:20.200
He's everything. Yeah.
Don't mess with it.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.701
-And you have to
keep up with him.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.901
But the spoiler alert is,
you can't keep up with him.

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:25.734
-No.
-So, we had him on the show.

00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:28.234
It was the second time
we had him on the show.

00:03:28.234 --> 00:03:31.634
The first time we had him
was 2015, I think.

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:34.167
But in 2018,
he sent me these shoes,

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.067
which was
a very rare collaboration

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:37.300
that he did with Jordan.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.167
He actually did
a Jordan collaboration

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:41.767
that's in stores last year,

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:43.234
but this was, like,
friends and family.

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:45.534
It showed up to
the Complex office once.

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.634
And super-rare pair.

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.234
I, like, checked.

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:50.868
In our sizes --
I know your size.

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:52.234
-Thank you.

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:54.501
-They're fetching
almost $25,000.

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:55.801
-What?!
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.934
-$25,000 for sneakers?
-Yeah.

00:03:57.934 --> 00:04:00.234
So it's, like,
a very special gift

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:02.467
that he gave me
out of my collection.

00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:04.334
And the "We the Best."
You know, that's his tagline.

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:07.267
And these are called
the Another One 3's.

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:10.167
If anyone knows --
If anyone knows Khaled,

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:12.501
that's one of
his many catchphrases.

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:16.400
-Yeah. I did a sneaker collab
with MSCHF.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.200
-I saw that.
-Do you know those guys?

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.467
-The Big Red Boots.
-Big Red Boots is MSCHF.

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.467
-Yes. Everyone know
the Big Red Boots?

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:23.801
How -- Did you guys see those?

00:04:23.801 --> 00:04:26.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
They're crushing it.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.267
-They're troublemakers.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:29.767
-Well, everyone says like,
"Oh, we want to disrupt."

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:31.601
They're real disruptors.

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.367
And you had --
you had your own collab

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:35.334
that you took super-serious.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:36.734
-I did.
-Yeah.

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:39.501
-I was very proud of these.
They're called Gobstompers.

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:42.167
And the idea of them were --
they're like Gobstoppers.

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:44.467
They're white sneakers,
but the more you wore them

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:46.434
and beat them up,
the colors would change

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:48.300
'cause there's different
layers of color.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.934
-Look at it.
-So this is my sneaker.

00:04:50.934 --> 00:04:54.667
And to be really honest,
you had --

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:56.300
-Yeah.
-You really have to --

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.467
[ Applause ]
Thank you.

00:04:57.467 --> 00:04:59.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:02.033
But this is them undistressed.

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:03.767
This is them
if you just wore them clean.

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:05.701
-Almost 20 years --
-And then this is -- But, yeah.

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.434
And this is what you do
if you mess them up.

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:10.834
But what I found out was they'll
never really look like this.

00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:13.534
You have to take, like,
a belt sander to them.

00:05:13.534 --> 00:05:15.400
-So that happens --
that happens a lot.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.667
A lot of brands are doing
pre-distressed sneakers,

00:05:17.667 --> 00:05:19.334
and you're like,
"Oh, these are --

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:21.300
I'm gonna wear them around
for a few days

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.968
and they're gonna
start peeling off."

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:25.234
You really have to
take, like, sandpaper to them

00:05:25.234 --> 00:05:26.934
for it to happen.
-This will never happen

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:28.667
unless you really take
a belt sander.

00:05:28.667 --> 00:05:31.133
-Years.
-It won't -- It will never ha--

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:33.501
They'll look like this.
That was the thing.

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:36.434
So really you get
a pair of these Gobstompers

00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:38.801
and get a belt sander and
then make them look like that.

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:40.300
And that's -- there you go.
They look cool.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.434
-But I love that you did that
because you're taught

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:45.167
